    "summary": "The model was repaired and now passes all L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nRoot cause: the instance layer held a stale girder count (n_girders = 4) and a corresponding bearing count (8), which contradicted the description (3 girders per span, 2 bearings per girder end → 6). This made every downstream formula recompute with the wrong multiplicity, so girder.A/I and support.*.bearing failed the L2-1 provenance/recomputation check. Correcting the instance (girder.count_per_span = 3, supports[*].bearing.per_girder_end = 2, with full bearing family data restored) fixed the formula inputs; the invalidated support decisions were then re-proposed.\n\nModel summary:\n- Structure: single simply supported span, 30 m (bearing centre lines), spine-beam 2D idealization.\n- Girders: 3 precast prestressed small-box girders per span, C40; combined section A = 3.417 m², I = 1.065 m⁴, Ec = 32500 MPa, γ = 26 kN/m³, w = 88.84 kN/m.\n- Bearings: plain laminated elastomeric at both abutments, 6 per support line (2 per girder end × 3 girders); a = 300 mm, b = 400 mm, 5 layers × 8 mm (te = 40 mm), Ge = 1.0 MPa; S = 10.71, Kv = 8.518e6 kN/m, Kh = 1.80e4 kN/m; longitudinal spring, rotational free.\n- Live load: Highway Class II, two-way, 2 design lanes, ξ = 1.0, qk = 7.875 kN/m², Pk = 240 kN.\n\nKey results:\n- f1 (first vertical bending) = 3.402 Hz → impact factor μ = 0.2006 (JTG D60-2015 4.3.2).\n- Self-weight: support reactions 1332.5 kN each; midspan moment 9994.1 kN·m.\n- Lane-load max positive moment (span 1) = 6449.6 kN·m."
